==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
Use [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]] or [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] to lock Mooth in place, then summon units that outrange him ([[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], etc.). You should be able to kill Mooth before Angelic Gory spawns, then it's an easy victory. It is also possible to rush this stage before the boss spawns, similar to Into the Future's [[NASA (Into the Future)|NASA]].

==='''Chapter 2 & 3'''===
If the Maawth isn't defeated by the time Angelic Gory or General GreGory arrives, then his wide area attacks will foil your plans to stack ranged attackers - at 1200%, this Maawth's 9,324 area damage is a lot even for Macho Legs to handle with his anti-Alien damage resistance, and the Gory variant will then push through the rest of your meatshields with relative ease, since he too has been buffed, to 200%.

For the rollout, try deploying a single Crazed Wall Cat at the start - it should meet up with Maawth in the middle of the field. You'll need to save up for something tanky (this may mean allowing for Maawth to hit the base. [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Dual]] [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Titans]] will do the trick, but if you are lucky enough to obtain [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Demon Cat]], you can throw him in instead because Greater Demon's extra knockbacks are made up for in raw attack power. Speaking of raw attack power, where's [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] when you need him? After Maawth is defeated, spam ranged attackers of your choice.

An alternative strategy is to spam [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] until the Maawth is dead and rush the enemy base with anything that has a decent speed. Doing this, you'll destroy the enemy base before or very soon after the Gory variant arrives.

